### =========================================================================
### IsoTreatment - requests for the Branch by Abstraction migration stack
###
### Stack:  docker compose up -d --build
###   @monolith :8080   the monolith - the address the frontend uses, before
###                     and after the migration; there is no gateway
###   Jaeger UI http://localhost:16686
###
### The API reads the JWT from an HttpOnly cookie named "token".
###
### To mint a token without going through registration (user id 1),
### run from the repository root:
###
###   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
###   b64u() { openssl base64 -A | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='; }
###   H=$(printf '%s' '{"alg":"HS256","typ":"JWT"}' | b64u)
###   P=$(printf '{"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/nameidentifier":"1","exp":%s,"iss":"isotreatment-users-issuer","aud":"isotreatment-users-audience"}' $(( $(date +%s) + 3600 )) | b64u)
###   S=$(printf '%s' "$H.$P" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$AUTHENTICATION_SIGNING_KEY" -binary | b64u)
###   echo "$H.$P.$S"
###
### The claim type is the full URI, not the short "nameid"; a token using
### "nameid" passes validation and then fails to yield a user id.
### =========================================================================

@monolith = http://localhost:8080
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE


### =========================================================================
### 1. Smoke tests - no authentication required
### =========================================================================

### Swagger is up  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/swagger/index.html

### No cookie  ->  401, proves authentication is wired
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder

### Unknown path  ->  404
GET {{monolith}}/nie-ma-takiej-sciezki

### Unknown credentials  ->  400 "Invalid username or password"
### A 500 here means the database is unreachable or migrations never ran.
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "brak@example.com",
  "password": "brak"
}


### =========================================================================
### 2. User lifecycle
###
### Registration sends a confirmation e-mail (SMTP settings come from .env)
### and leaves EmailConfirmed = false, so login fails until the account is
### confirmed. For local work it is easier to seed a user with SQL and mint
### a token (see the header of this file).
### =========================================================================

### Register  ->  200
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jan",
  "lastName": "Kowalski",
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "Haslo123!",
  "confirmPassword": "Haslo123!",
  "weight": 70,
  "climaxDoseInMiligramsPerKilogramOfBodyWeight": 120,
  "dailyDose": 40,
  "medicationStartDate": "2024-01-01T00:00:00"
}

### Confirm the e-mail (token arrives by e-mail)
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/confirmEmail?emailConfirmationToken=PASTE_CONFIRMATION_TOKEN

### Log in - the JWT comes back in a Set-Cookie header, not in the body
# @name login
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "Haslo123!"
}

### Current user  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/api/user/info
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Update the current user  ->  200
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/info/update
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "firstName": "Jan",
  "lastName": "Nowak",
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "weight": 72,
  "climaxDoseInMiligramsPerKilogramOfBodyWeight": 120,
  "dailyDose": 40
}

### Log out - clears the cookie
POST {{monolith}}/api/user/logout
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 3. Reminders
###
### This is the slice being extracted into the Treatment service. The same
### requests keep working unchanged through every phase: after the switch
### the monolith forwards them to the Treatment service behind
### IReminderGateway, and nothing here should notice.
### Note: POST returns 200 with no Location header, not 201.
### Time serializes as "08:00" (pl-PL culture), not "08:00:00".
### =========================================================================

### List  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Create  ->  200 {"id":N,"time":"08:00"}
POST {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "08:00"
}

### Read one  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder/1
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Update  ->  200
PUT {{monolith}}/api/reminder/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "time": "21:15"
}

### Delete  ->  204 with an empty body
DELETE {{monolith}}/api/reminder/1
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Missing reminder  ->  404 "Reminder not found", plain text, no Content-Type
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder/999999
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 4. Diary entries
### =========================================================================

### List  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/api/entry
Cookie: token={{token}}

### Create  ->  200
POST {{monolith}}/api/entry
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "content": "Skin looks better, no side effects today.",
  "date": "2026-08-28T00:00:00"
}

### Update  ->  200
PUT {{monolith}}/api/entry/1
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: token={{token}}

{
  "content": "Corrected note."
}

### Delete  ->  204
DELETE {{monolith}}/api/entry/1
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 5. Treatment process calculation
### =========================================================================

### Stateless calculation from the user's pharmacological parameters  ->  200
GET {{monolith}}/api/treatment-process
Cookie: token={{token}}


### =========================================================================
### 6. CORS preflight
### =========================================================================

### Preflight  ->  204 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://localhost:5173
OPTIONS {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET


### =========================================================================
### 7. Authentication edge cases
### =========================================================================

### Token in the Authorization header instead of the cookie  ->  500
### JwtBearer falls back to the header and authenticates the request, but the
### controller then reads the token from the cookie again and passes null to
### ITokenService. This is why the monolith has to accept the cookie from the
### frontend, while the Treatment service will read only the header the
### monolith sets when it forwards the call.
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Malformed token  ->  401
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token=not.a.jwt


### =========================================================================
### 8. Generating traffic for Jaeger
###
### Fire this, then open http://localhost:16686 and pick the "monolith"
### service. Before the switch the trace is monolith -> one SQL query. After
### it, the same request should show monolith -> HTTP call -> Treatment
### service -> SQL, all in ONE trace. Two unlinked traces mean the
### traceparent header is not propagated by the HttpClient that
### TreatmentServiceReminderGateway uses.
### =========================================================================

### Served in-process by the monolith
GET {{monolith}}/api/reminder
Cookie: token={{token}}
